# Euler CRM regression guard

These rules are the ones recent fixes kept breaking. Check them before changing OEM sync, variant save, delivery, scheme, or pack price.

## Dealer body vs OEM invoice

- A variant saved in Euler sets `oemSkuConfirmed`. Later OEM sync and Mark Delivered leave that model, variant, body type, and price in place.
- The invoice body is stored on `oemBilledModel`, `oemBilledVariant`, and `oemBilledBodyType`. The drawer says which body OEM billed and which body was billed to the customer.
- A chassis nobody has confirmed still takes its own invoice body. One unit's body is never copied onto a sibling.
- A Coulson yard-body to invoice-body change (built FB, billed DV) still follows the invoice when the dealer has not confirmed a different body.
- Confirming a body is not an adoption. Do not run the Price Master reprice callback unless the working variant actually changed.
- Mark Delivered stamps the selected unit after the OEM patch is built. The final write must keep those delivery flags. Overlay names and labels onto the stamped units. Do not replace the unit list with the pre-stamp snapshot.
- Saving the current variant on a locked or delivered file still goes through the file lock. Showroom Admin cannot confirm a body on a delivered file.

## Price

- OEM billed date (`soldDate` on the unit, then the file) decides which list price applies — same order as scheme month. Booking date is only the fallback when nothing is billed yet.
- Coulson sync writes today's Turbo list into Price Master. For an OEM billed day before 1 Sep 2026, peel the ₹15,000 Turbo uplift only when that sync itself is on/after 1 Sep — an August sync already stored the August list.
- Opening Price Structure must not keep today's synced master on an August-billed file. A real booked figure that already matches the billed day (or is not today's sync) stays. A later pack unit without its own ex does not inherit Unit 1's header price.
- Pack rebuild prices each unit from its own OEM billed date. A September-billed extra unit on an August booking keeps the September list.
- Saving RTO or insurance on a booked pack unit must keep that unit's billed-day ex-showroom. A same-variant billed-day list correction must not clear Cx Demand. Preview and save use the same booked-price rule for every unit, not only Unit 1.
- ASM / RM field view does not get Price Structure or stored deal prices.
- A pack unit already paid in full keeps that payable when only the body name changes, including when Cx Demand was not already locked.
- An unpaid unit takes the new variant's Price Master price, and the previous Cx Demand does not stay on it.
- A lower RTO or insurance does not reduce Gross Vehicle Cost while a customer price is locked.
- A scheme amount changes the price only after someone selects that scheme.
- Turbo list uplift applies from 1 Sep 2026 only when Price Master has never been OEM-synced. Synced rows are the OEM invoice base.

## OEM sync

- Coulson sign-in posts to `https://coulson.eulerlogistics.com/api/v1/login` with Basic `username:SHA256(password):coulson` and an empty body. The typed password and the old `euler-auth` host are both refused.
- Chassis, invoice, and plate still come from Coulson for the chassis on the file.
- A different model family is not written on as a body change.
- After the whole file is delivered, the working variant stays until someone chooses Use billed body + price.

- `_is_todays_synced_list` is true only for a Coulson-synced row (`oemSyncedAt`). On an unsynced catalog row the raw base is a valid booked price. (Regressed by PR #307, restored; guard: `test_deal_pass_meet_cx.py::test_pack_rto_insurance_cut_shrinks_additional_not_payable`, `regression_claude/test_approved_invariants.py::test_rto_edit_never_moves_saved_ex_on_unsynced_turbo_row`.)

## Booking and Price Master (PR #11, #12, #13)

- Booking needs a Price Master row; the API answers 422 otherwise and the lead stays New.
- The Convert to Booking drawer keeps Confirm disabled while the price preview loads and when Price Master has no row. (Lost in PR #215 `2592d1e`, restored; guard: `frontend/src/pages/BookEnquiryDrawer.test.js` "PR #12 guard" tests.)
- A booked file keeps its booked price when Price Master changes later.

## Money

- Customer receipt: amount > 0; above Customer Payable → 422 unless `allowExcess`; identical receipt within 4 s → 409; non-cash needs a reference (PR #4, #55, #162, U4).
- `totalReceived` equals the sum of payment rows; `customerOutstanding = customerPayable − totalReceived` (never negative; surplus is `excessReceived`).
- Finance-mode receipt moves outstanding from customer to financer; the financer's disbursement does not change customer outstanding (PR #15, #55).
- Claim and financer receipts: duplicate → 409, beyond the eligible / committed amount → 422, total and receipt list written together (CLD-06). The frontend never auto-retries `/leads/{id}/payments|refund|convert-booking`, `/claims/receipt`, `/finance/{file}/receipt`, or `POST /leads`.
- Sales GM never posts customer or Finance receipts (PR #94; regressed 27 Sep `070836e`, restored CLD-13).
- Delivery needs a cleared customer outstanding and the full checklist; Close needs a reason, and a delivered close needs RC + number plate (PRD Iteration 8-9; guard: `regression_claude/test_approved_invariants.py`).

## Scheme and dealer earnings

- Scheme month = OEM billed date, then explicit date, then booking date; last month never carries forward.
- Eligibility is not assignment; company share is applied first; an unused component gives no OEM claim and no retained income (PR #20, #21, #33).
- Customer-passed benefit is never dealer-retained income. Dealer total on the lead equals the Dealer Earnings report row (guard: `regression_claude/test_cld10_cld24_reset_and_earnings.py`).
- Insurance payout is a separate ledger; MIS upload overwrites expected payout only when uploaded (PR #119, chat T265).

## Lead data safety

- No GET request and no boot job deletes or merges leads. Duplicate cleanup is owner-only, dry-run first, archived and audited (CLD-01; regressed by `f1e648e`).
- `PUT /leads/{id}` is a partial update (PR #3).
- A different 10-digit mobile is a different customer even with the same name (PR #286).
- Go-live reset also clears lead-keyed KYC, WhatsApp and lead requests (CLD-10).

## Roles and privacy

- Staff payloads (lead, list, 360, previews) never carry owner P&L keys: `OWNER_PNL_LEAD_KEYS`, `OWNER_PNL_COMMERCIAL_KEYS`, `OWNER_PNL_SHARE_KEYS`, and `oemExtraSupport.dealerRetained`. (360 view leaked `oemExtraSupportRetained` until this fix; guard: `test_staff_payloads_never_carry_owner_pnl_keys`.)
- Executives see only their own leads; dealer earnings and owner reports are owner-only; insurance and manual claims are money-desk only (PR #41).
- The public share board returns counts only, no names (CLD-02). Webhooks without a configured secret write nothing (CLD-07). No plaintext passwords are stored or returned (CLD-04).

## Process (why #307 shipped a money regression)

- "Critical regression" failed on `main` for PR #307 and the PR was merged anyway. Never merge with a red `critical-regression`, `backend-full` or `frontend-tests` check.
- When a test that guards money fails, fix the code or get the owner's written approval to change the rule. Do not edit the expected amount to make it green.
- Before editing a shared pricing helper (`_turbo_selling_ex`, `_stored_ex_matches_row`, `_is_todays_synced_list`, `_saved_ex_for_preview`, `_reprice_pack_deal`, `set_price_structure`, `price_preview`), run `test_deal_pass_meet_cx.py`, `test_turbo_sept_exshowroom_uplift.py`, `test_same_order_multi_unit.py`, `test_rto_insurance_deal_approval.py` and `tests/regression_claude/`.

## Added 25 Nov 2026 (verified against code, tests and production)

- Convert to Booking judges "dealer discount" on the requested booking date, the same date the price was filled for. A back-dated booking with no discount is not parked for approval. (`convert_booking` → `_require_booking_deal_approval`; guard: `test_scheme_retained_and_step_locks.py::test_booking_autofill_does_not_lock_price_for_staff`.)
- WhatsApp model-interest replies are numbered against the menu the customer received (`lead.modelAskMenu`), never against today's Price Master list. (guard: `test_iter33_model_ask.py`.)
- BotSpace webhook: with no secret saved, callbacks are processed (inbox, delivery status, opt-out). With a secret saved (Settings → WhatsApp → Webhook secret, or `BOTSPACE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) it is required via `?secret=` or `x-botspace-secret`. Never drop unsigned callbacks silently. Exotel stays fail-closed. (guard: `regression_claude/test_cld07_webhooks.py`.)
- OEM "Sold, PDI pending": read-only pull (`vehicle_status=SOLD`, `is_pdi_done=false`), stored without customer name/phone, replaced only on a complete pull. (guard: `test_oem_pdi_pending.py`.)
- Price Master reprice: owner edits reach live Active, unsettled, not-delivered leads booked on/after 1 Sep; OEM-sourced rows keep Coulson's ex-showroom. (guard: `test_iter27_price_master_reprice.py`.)
- Only the Scheme Claim Register is written to the live Google Sheet (`LIVE_SHEET_ENTITIES`).

## Test discipline

- Tests never reach live services: Google Sheets is blocked by `conftest.py` (modules that test sync logic use `pytestmark = pytest.mark.fake_sheets` with an in-memory fake); Coulson fetches are stubbed by name; a new Coulson fetch needs a conftest stub.
- Run the backend suite with `python scripts/run_tests_isolated.py` (one process per module). Modules share one in-memory DB through `server`; a single process makes results order-dependent.
- A test that fails after a rule change is updated only with a comment naming the PR/commit that changed the rule. Never weaken a money assertion to get green.
